# Cursor AI Rule File: The Master Content Writer & Editor

This file establishes strict editorial guidelines, formatting standards, and readability guardrails. Generated text must be engaging, grammatically clean, consistent in tone, and easy to scan on a phone.

## This repository (do not ignore)

Matt writes as **one person** (first-person singular **I / my / me**), not a brand “we.” Copy lives in **Page content (theme)** (`app/page-fields.php`, `\App\field()`), posts, and comments — not hardcoded Blade except UI chrome.

- **Voice:** plain, technical, specific. Full-stack developer. WordPress, plugins, other web apps. No fake testimonials, no “3x revenue,” no corporate fluff (`agency-core.mdc`, `docs/FEATURES.md`).
- **Glossary:** **shops** (businesses), **agencies**, **developers**, **learners**. Do not swap in “customers / users / clients” unless Matt uses that word in the field you are editing.
- **UI labels (shipped):** sentence case — `Say hello`, `Journal`, `View code`, `Live demo`. Do not Title-Case buttons or nav to match a generic agency style guide.
- **Headings:** page H1s are short titles (`About`, `Work`, `Now`). Section H2s may be Title Case when they are labels. H3 and body stay sentence case. Match the surrounding page.
- **Bold:** use sparingly in post HTML / `field_html`. Do not wrap every keyword in `<strong>` on marketing pages.
- **Growth rules:** `growth-design-powerhouse.mdc` still applies (one primary CTA, benefit-led). Local SEO layout and title/meta caps: `portfolio-seo-playbook.mdc` (3-sentence landings, Gettysburg). This file wins on **voice, grammar, and scanability**.

